1
00:00:18,454 --> 00:00:22,775
[SPEAKER_01]: So, this is a sutta from the Anguttara Nikaya.

2
00:00:24,375 --> 00:00:26,696
[SPEAKER_01]: We've done this before, this one.

3
00:00:27,276 --> 00:00:28,096
[SPEAKER_01]: Just do it again.

4
00:00:31,175 --> 00:00:36,438
[SPEAKER_01]: Bhikkhus, I will teach you a dhamma exposition on union and disengagement.

5
00:00:37,759 --> 00:00:41,482
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll just go with the man's description.

6
00:00:42,993 --> 00:00:58,104
[SPEAKER_01]: A man, bhikkhus, attends internally to his masculine faculty, his masculine comportment, his masculine appearance, his masculine aspect, his masculine desire, his masculine voice, his masculine ornamentation.

7
00:00:59,344 --> 00:01:02,467
[SPEAKER_01]: He becomes excited by these and takes delight in them.

8
00:01:03,267 --> 00:01:09,712
[SPEAKER_01]: Excited by them and taking delight in them, he attends externally to a woman's feminine faculty.

9
00:01:10,092 --> 00:01:11,073
[SPEAKER_01]: To the counterpart.

10
00:01:12,252 --> 00:01:15,894
[SPEAKER_01]: And so, he becomes excited by these and takes delight in them.

11
00:01:16,534 --> 00:01:20,416
[SPEAKER_01]: Excited by them, taking delight in them, he desires union externally.

12
00:01:21,196 --> 00:01:25,138
[SPEAKER_01]: And he also desires the pleasure and joy that arise on account of such union.

13
00:01:26,019 --> 00:01:30,921
[SPEAKER_01]: Beings who are delighted with their masculinity enter upon union with women.

14
00:01:31,661 --> 00:01:36,584
[SPEAKER_01]: It is in this way that a man does not transcend his masculinity.

15
00:01:37,324 --> 00:01:39,225
[SPEAKER_01]: This is how union comes about.

16
00:01:42,130 --> 00:01:44,051
[SPEAKER_01]: And how does disengagement come about?

17
00:01:44,872 --> 00:01:47,774
