354
00:30:27,163 --> 00:30:32,246
[SPEAKER_01]: And the more you go, you try that... Well, the more... Yeah, exactly.

355
00:30:32,327 --> 00:30:36,830
[SPEAKER_02]: The more confined you become, the more burdened by your dependence on sensuality you become.

356
00:30:39,730 --> 00:30:48,185
[SPEAKER_02]: That's why it's important to realize that this needs to be lived on the level of enduring the pressure, not acting out of it, calming your mind within it,

357
00:30:49,959 --> 00:31:06,290
[SPEAKER_02]: So, withdrawal from the dependence on the pleasure of the assumed external kind is the prerequisite for that pleasure of jhāna, that genuine release of the burden, of the debt, of crossing the desert, all the similes the Buddha gave for the pleasure of first jhāna.

358
00:31:06,730 --> 00:31:07,991
[SPEAKER_01]: Withdrawing from...

359
00:31:08,031 --> 00:31:13,235
[SPEAKER_02]: It's withdrawing from the unwholesome, withdrawing from the wrong order that you've been assuming.

360
00:31:13,915 --> 00:31:14,756
[SPEAKER_02]: That's your work.

361
00:31:15,476 --> 00:31:18,598
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, the release will occur, as a result of it, of the right kind.

362
00:31:18,698 --> 00:31:21,739
[SPEAKER_02]: That would be the true opening amidst the confinement.

363
00:31:22,259 --> 00:31:27,662
[SPEAKER_02]: But people don't want to deal with the confinement, don't want to deal with the pressure, don't want to deal with the enduring it.

364
00:31:27,982 --> 00:31:38,848
[SPEAKER_02]: They want a technique that will get them the experience of pleasure, that they will then take to be jhāna, and then assume that all this work has been done on account of this special meditation pleasure that they had.

365
00:31:39,895 --> 00:31:45,560
[SPEAKER_02]: And as I said many times, that's exactly mirroring principle of the sensuality that you've been chasing and acting out of.

366
00:31:46,400 --> 00:31:53,446
[SPEAKER_02]: Now, just instead of that, you're watching your nostrils or whatever else, but you're still seeking for that pleasant thing to be your escape.

367
00:31:54,487 --> 00:31:54,627
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

368
00:31:54,967 --> 00:32:00,752
[SPEAKER_02]: The escape is found by not becoming, not being, not maintaining the dependence upon the wrong order.

369
00:32:01,914 --> 00:32:03,634
[SPEAKER_02]: And then the pleasure of jhāna will happen.

370
00:32:03,994 --> 00:32:10,536
[SPEAKER_02]: Having been quite withdrawn from central pleasures, he abides and dwells and experiences pleasure of withdrawal.

371
00:32:11,636 --> 00:32:14,537
[SPEAKER_02]: And then he enters and abides in the first jhānas.

372
00:32:14,717 --> 00:32:16,217
[SPEAKER_02]: That's how sūtas describe it.

373
00:32:17,157 --> 00:32:27,280
[SPEAKER_02]: Not having been withdrawn, still being pressured by sensuality, he gets a technique, he enters jhāna, and all this just falls off, and senses disappear, and it's a magical experience.

374
00:32:27,320 --> 00:32:29,260
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, well, good luck with that one.

375
00:32:34,965 --> 00:32:36,927
[SPEAKER_01]: As soon as you wake up from that, boom!

376
00:32:37,307 --> 00:32:38,708
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, it needs to be practical.

377
00:32:38,748 --> 00:32:42,751
[SPEAKER_02]: And if you think, okay, so the second jhāna, the third jhāna, again, that's what Buddha said.

378
00:32:42,772 --> 00:32:51,999
[SPEAKER_02]: It's like a cow that hasn't even established itself upon the first rock it stepped on, planned, yeah, started planning to step on the second one and falls between the two.

379
00:32:52,540 --> 00:32:58,785
[SPEAKER_02]: So, refrain from thinking about perception, neither perception, no perception, and the basis of infinite space and everything else.

380
00:32:59,425 --> 00:33:12,550
[SPEAKER_02]: Until you have been quite withdrawn from sensuality and have experienced at least that first basic okasa of first jhāna, of complete relinquishment of ownership and subsiding of unwholesome states.

381
00:33:15,651 --> 00:33:18,172
[SPEAKER_02]: When there is no more basis for the perversion of the order.

382
00:33:19,152 --> 00:33:20,493
[SPEAKER_02]: That's why jhāna is so wholesome.

